"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-18T09:22:39Z","updated_at":"2026-09-18T09:22:39Z","body":"Rebased.\r\nSeems like Snap Settings were already handled by another PR (#106684) and it used EditorSpinSliders. Not sure which one is preferred.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5727978531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5823742129","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111588#issuecomment-5823742129","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111588","id":5823742129,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWx9AsQ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T23:09:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T23:09:58Z","body":"> Seems like Snap Settings were already handled by another PR (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106684) and it used EditorSpinSliders. Not sure which one is preferred.\r\n\r\nI think we should standardize around EditorSpinSlider when in the editor.\r\n\r\n@passivestar Thoughts? SpinBox can be situationally better thanks to its up/down buttons, but having an easier ability to drag the value (or the slider below it) is probably more valuable.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5823742129/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5825511354","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111588#issuecomment-5825511354","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111588","id":5825511354,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWzo_ug","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-25T02:08:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-25T02:08:11Z","body":"> @passivestar Thoughts? SpinBox can be situationally better thanks to its up/down buttons, but having an easier ability to drag the value (or the slider below it) is probably more valuable.\r\n\r\nYeah, spinbox-style inputs mostly make sense for small integers, i.e when you're ordering food in a mobile app and want to change the amount of sauces from 1 to 3. In a game engine it's usually big numbers and float numbers so it would makes sense to prefer draggable `EditorSpinSlider`s, especially in this transform popup ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5825511354/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]